 It throws an `Error` when the patch is invalid, or when one of its operations fails, such as a `remove` of
 a missing member or a `test` that does not match. The error names the operation index, and the input is
 left unchanged.
+
+## JSON Merge Patch
+
+`applyMergePatch(target, patch)` applies a JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7386) to a JSON document. A patch object
+merges into the target: a member set to `null` is removed, any other member is merged recursively, and an
+array replaces the target's value. A patch that is not an object replaces the whole document. It returns
+the merged document as a new value: neither the target nor the patch is modified.
+
+```ts
+import { applyMergePatch } from './src/index.ts';
+
+applyMergePatch({ title: 'Old', author: { name: 'Ann' }, draft: true }, {
+  title: 'New',
+  author: { name: null },
+  draft: null,
+}); // { title: 'New', author: {} }
+```
+
+It does not throw: every JSON value is a valid merge patch.
