+---
+id: task-004-implement-json-merge-patch-rfc-7386-as-applymergepatch
+type: task
+title: "Implement JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7386) as applyMergePatch"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Some of our clients send partial updates in the simpler JSON Merge Patch format. Implement JSON Merge Patch,
+as specified in RFC 7386. Export `applyMergePatch(target, patch)` from `src/index.ts`: it applies a merge
+patch to a target JSON document and returns the merged document.
+
+## Design
+
+Recorded in dl-007 (RFC 7386 semantics: `null` removes a member, objects merge recursively, other values
+replace) and dl-008 (a new document is returned, inputs are never mutated, and no error is thrown). Both are
+submitted and wait for approval.
+
+## What was done
+
+- `test/merge-patch.test.ts`: written first. It covers the 15 RFC 7386 Appendix A examples, a non-object
+  patch replacing the target, `null` removing and not creating members, arrays replacing rather than
+  merging, nested merges, the no-mutation guarantee, a member named `__proto__`, and an inherited name such
+  as `constructor`. Run before the implementation existed, it failed with "does not provide an export named
+  'applyMergePatch'".
+- `src/index.ts`: `applyMergePatch`, with doc comments, and a private `mergeInto` helper. The target is
+  deep-copied once, and the helper merges into that copy, as `applyPatch` does (dl-003). It reuses the
+  `isRecord` and `defineMember` helpers.
+- `README.md`: a short usage section for `applyMergePatch`, with an example checked by running it.
+
+## Verification
+
+- `npm test`: 103 of 103 pass (76 existing, 27 new).
+- `tsc -p tsconfig.json --noEmit` (TypeScript 5.9.3, strict mode, from outside the repo, not added as a
+  dependency): no errors in `src`.
+
+## Open
+
+- dl-006 (plain JSON data) still waits for approval. `applyMergePatch` does not check that its patch is
+  plain JSON data; once dl-006 is approved, the same check should apply here too (dl-008 says so).
